# EigenScript gap: strings are NUL-terminated, so a string cannot hold byte 0
# (EigenScript#1286 row "The string model": bytes vs text decided).
# Lua:      #"a\0b" -> 3, string.char(0) -> a 1-byte string
# Expected: byte strings that hold any byte, as Lua's do (len 3 below).
# Actual v0.44.0:  str_from_bytes stops at the NUL (len 1), and chr of 0
#           raises.
# Rows: str_embedded_nul, str_len, str_byte_char_sub_rep (D).
s is str_from_bytes of [97, 0, 98]
print of (len of s)
try:
    print of (len of (chr of 0))
catch e:
    print of e.message
